        "name": "For the choux pastry",
        "sourceIndex": 0,
        "steps": [
          {
            "sourceIndex": 0,
            "text": "Preheat the oven to 200°C (thermostat 6/7). Cover a baking sheet with parchment paper.",
            "mediaId": null
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 1,
            "text": "In a saucepan, put the butter and salt. Bring to a boil. When the butter is completely melted, remove the pan from the heat.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:759"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 2,
            "text": "Add flour and mix well.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:825"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 3,
            "text": "The dough should form a ball.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:839"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 4,
            "text": "Add the eggs one by one. Mix well.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:842"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 5,
            "text": "The dough should be smooth and not stick to the edges of the pan.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:838"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 6,
            "text": "Using a spoon or a pastry bag, form small heaps of dough on the baking sheet, separating them from each other as the puffs will double in size during cooking.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:831"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 7,
            "text": "Bake at 200°C for 10-15 minutes. Then lower the temperature to 180°C (thermostat 6) and cook for another 10 minutes or so until you get a nice golden color. Remove the puffs from the oven and let cool.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:827"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "For the cream",
        "sourceIndex": 1,
        "steps": [
          {
            "sourceIndex": 0,
            "text": "In a small saucepan, blanch the egg with the sugar.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:836"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 1,
            "text": "Add milk and vanilla. Place over very low heat. Stirring constantly, bring to a boil. Remove from heat and let cool. Remove the vanilla pod.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:828"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 2,
            "text": "In the bowl of a mixer, cream the butter. While continuing to mix, gradually incorporate the milk and sugar preparation.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:824"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 3,
            "text": "Make an incision in the choux. Using a teaspoon or a pastry bag, fill them with the cream. Sprinkle with icing sugar.",
            "mediaId": null
          }
        ]
      }
